# Trivy baseline — Phase 16.7
#
# These are PRE-EXISTING high advisories in direct dependencies that cannot be
# cleared without a MAJOR upgrade. They are listed here so the Trivy gate
# blocks NEW findings instead of failing forever on known debt.
#
#   nodemailer  9.1.1 -> 10.x   (breaking; the mail module was rewritten in 21.4)
#   fastify     5.12.5         (npm reports no 5.x fix at all for these)
#
# Two more were NOT baselined, because they had non-breaking fixes and are
# fixed in the lockfile by this branch:
#
#   @nestjs/platform-fastify  11.2.1 -> 11.2.7  (GHSA-9c5c-9qcx-q35q, a
#       path-scoped middleware bypass — an auth bypass)
#   sharp  0.35.2 -> 0.35.5                    (GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w / CVE-2026-96889,
#       the librsvg CVE)
#
# Trivy reports some of these by CVE and some by GHSA depending on the advisory
# source, so both spellings are listed.
#
# Re-baseline each of these the day its upgrade merges, and delete the lines.
# Reviewed 2026-10-12.

